jobs.description:
As an Administrative Customs Coordinator, you play a vital role in ensuring international shipments cross borders smoothly and comply with customs regulations. You will be responsible for processing customs declarations accurately and ensuring all documentation meets legal requirements. No customs experience? No problem. DHL provides comprehensive training and offers a Junior Broker Course, allowing you to build a successful career in the customs and logistics industry.

What You'll Do

- Prepare, process, and monitor customs declarations;
- Review and verify shipment documentation for accuracy and compliance;
- Track and manage the progress of customs files and declarations;
- Communicate with customers, colleagues, and external stakeholders;
- Identify and resolve administrative discrepancies;
- Follow customs procedures and applicable regulations to ensure compliance;

- Strong attention to detail and accuracy;
-  Excellent organizational and administrative skills;
-  Good command of the English language, both written and spoken;
-  Strong communication and problem-solving abilities;
-  Experience in administration, logistics, customer service, or a related field is an advantage, but not required;
-  A proactive attitude and willingness to learn.

Are you looking for a warehouse job in an international team with clear working hours and opportunities to grow? Start as a Warehouse Employee at GXO Logistics in Tilburg. You earn €14.99 gross per hour and receive travel allowance and pension.

You work with clothing and accessories. Depending on your department, you collect, pack, check or move products.

Your tasks can include:

- Picking orders with a scanner;
- Packing and checking products;
- Processing returned items;
- Receiving and storing products;
- Preparing orders for shipment;
- Keeping your workplace clean and safe.

You will receive training for the tasks in your department. There are also opportunities to learn different warehouse processes.

You work either a fixed morning shift or in two shifts:

- Morning shift: 06:00 to 14:45;
- Afternoon shift: 15:15 to 00:00.

You like active work and enjoy working together with others.

We ask:

- You speak English at B1 level or higher;
- You are physically fit and can stand and walk for longer periods;
- You are available for a fixed morning shift or two-shift schedule;
- You have your own accommodation and transport;
- You can apply for a Certificate of Good Conduct (VOG);
- You are available full-time.

Experience in a warehouse is useful, but not listed as a requirement for this job.
